1
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,860
Wanna go take a look around?

2
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,380
(Group date for five)
Sure.

3
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:18,840
Let's walk around.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:22,280
What kind of place is this?

5
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:24,060
(Taking photos)

6
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:26,520
So can we come in at night?

7
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:31,280
I'll spray on some bug repellent first.

8
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:31,840
Okay.

9
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,520
Why does this feel
like spraying perfume?

10
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:42,800
"Attacks" from both sides.

11
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:47,760
I'll do the same too.

12
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:48,480
Learning from you.

13
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,400
Why'd you walk straight into it?

14
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,480
Got a whole mouthful.

15
00:00:58,480 --> 00:00:59,520
Putting it right into practice.

16
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:01,200
How'd you do that backward thing?

17
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,080
Just spray from behind.

18
00:01:02,080 --> 00:01:02,840
Then walk backward.

19
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:07,600
(Backing up together)
Backward.

20
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:08,160
Right.

21
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:09,600
Nice.

22
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:16,360
- Why are there still mosquitoes?
- You okay?

23
00:01:16,360 --> 00:01:17,680
They keep flying into my eyes.

24
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:19,120
I'll block them.

25
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:22,120
I'll block them.

26
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:26,400
A human wall.

27
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,620
(Smiles)

28
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:32,840
That's so random.

29
00:01:36,260 --> 00:01:36,900
(Glances)

30
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:44,200
When was the last time you went camping,

31
00:01:44,200 --> 00:01:45,120
Yu Yang?

32
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,680
I actually go camping a lot.

33
00:01:47,120 --> 00:01:47,760
Pretty often?

34
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:49,600
I love having barbecues by the river.

35
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:51,080
Me?

36
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,760
It's probably been a few years.

37
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:55,480
That's okay. We can do this more often.

38
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,200
That'd be great.

39
00:01:56,200 --> 00:01:56,560
Yeah.

40
00:01:56,560 --> 00:01:57,800
The last time I had a barbecue

41
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:58,840
was the last time.

42
00:01:58,840 --> 00:01:59,720
The last time?

43
00:02:01,840 --> 00:02:02,720
This side should be good.

44
00:02:02,720 --> 00:02:03,680
Let's add another piece.

45
00:02:04,360 --> 00:02:05,200
And over there.

46
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:07,080
You have to light them one by one.

47
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,400
I...

48
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:09,360
Why don't you give it to me?

49
00:02:09,360 --> 00:02:10,199
I'll get that...

50
00:02:10,199 --> 00:02:11,160
Like this, right?

51
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:15,040
Now I wanna learn how to barbecue.

52
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,000
It takes some skill.

53
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,040
You're always learning. That's normal.

54
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:21,760
Okay.

55
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,720
Now let's fan it a bit.

56
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,560
Look, the fire's starting up.

57
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,000
It's going.

58
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:32,840
It's starting up.

59
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,040
Come on, Fang.

60
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:36,520
Go.

61
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:40,040
What's that sound?

62
00:02:40,800 --> 00:02:42,560
Probably a mosquito getting "fried".

63
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:44,120
Grilled mosquito.

64
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:46,040
(Cracks up)

65
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:46,840
A little "bonus snack".

66
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,560
The sun's already set.

67
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,080
It'll be dark soon.

68
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:57,200
Do you guys prefer sunsets or sunrises?

69
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,040
(Asks)

70
00:02:58,040 --> 00:02:59,440
I think I prefer

71
00:02:59,440 --> 00:03:00,120
sunsets.

72
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:00,760
Why?

73
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,120
Sunsets just feel prettier.

74
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:04,080
They're just prettier?

75
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,120
Sunrises are beautiful too.

76
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:11,520
Sunsets have more of a vibe.

77
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:12,280
Yeah.

78
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:13,600
Do you like...

79
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:15,000
Do you like sunrises more?

80
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,440
I prefer sunsets.

81
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:17,960
I think we all prefer sunsets.

82
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:18,560
Same answer as you.

83
00:03:20,360 --> 00:03:21,200
Because I feel like

84
00:03:21,200 --> 00:03:22,160
when you see the sunrise,

85
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:22,600
it means

86
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,400
another busy day is starting.

87
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,680
That sense of stress comes right back.

88
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:28,680
But with a sunset,

89
00:03:28,680 --> 00:03:30,080
when you see it,

90
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:31,960
it gives you this sense

91
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:32,880
of belonging.

92
00:03:32,880 --> 00:03:33,920
Yeah, a sense of belonging.

93
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,640
It's like after a lifetime of hard work,

94
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:36,200
sometimes

95
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,720
the best part comes at the end.

96
00:03:44,400 --> 00:03:45,560
This shrimp's for you.

97
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,480
Have it.

98
00:03:47,480 --> 00:03:48,560
I noticed you haven't eaten much.

99
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,360
You don't eat fatty meat,

100
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:49,800
or lamb.

101
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:51,200
So maybe have more seafood.

102
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:52,680
I think you might like this.

103
00:03:53,080 --> 00:03:53,880
Okay.

104
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:59,080
These are the little sushi rolls
Yu Yang brought.

105
00:03:59,400 --> 00:04:00,720
Wanna try some first?

106
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,000
Sure.

107
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,120
You go first.

108
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:03,360
You eat first.

109
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,040
Let's split them up.

110
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:06,260
- Okay, thanks.
- I think...

111
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:07,080
I think this one's beef.

112
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:07,560
Okay.

113
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,080
Okay, thanks.

114
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,040
Thanks for bringing these, Yu Yang.

115
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,040
Thanks.

116
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:12,920
It's okay. You guys pick first.

117
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:13,880
See which one you like.

118
00:04:13,880 --> 00:04:15,000
Can I just grab one with my hand?

119
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:15,360
Sure.

120
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,760
Which one do you want?

121
00:04:18,040 --> 00:04:19,079
You pick first. It's fine.

122
00:04:19,079 --> 00:04:20,120
You go first.

123
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:21,600
Thanks.

124
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:23,240
Okay, I'll take this one.

125
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:27,160
Sun Bohan.

126
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:27,680
What?

127
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:28,800
Here, give me your plate.

128
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,240
My plate?

129
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:30,480
Here.

130
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:30,840
Thanks.

131
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,840
I don't think I grilled this

132
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:33,160
potato

133
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,040
very well.

134
00:04:34,360 --> 00:04:35,160
Looks pretty good.

135
00:04:35,160 --> 00:04:35,640
Pretty good?

136
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:37,200
But at least

137
00:04:37,200 --> 00:04:38,080
it doesn't look

138
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:39,080
like it has any

139
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:39,760
weird colors.

140
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:40,520
Just put them on one plate.

141
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,240
They can grab them with chopsticks.

142
00:04:43,280 --> 00:04:44,320
Your potatoes.

143
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:46,840
Don't touch it with that glove.

144
00:04:47,160 --> 00:04:47,720
Okay.

145
00:04:48,200 --> 00:04:49,960
You can give me the shrimp.

146
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:50,760
I've got gloves on.

147
00:04:50,760 --> 00:04:51,680
I'll peel them for you.

148
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,480
Thanks.

149
00:04:54,400 --> 00:04:55,000
This one's...

150
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:55,680
There's one more.

151
00:04:55,680 --> 00:04:56,240
It's Chen Hewen's.

152
00:04:56,240 --> 00:04:56,640
It's fine.

153
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:58,280
I'll just eat it with the shell.

154
00:04:58,280 --> 00:04:59,240
You eat the shell too?

155
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,060
They say it's good for calcium.

156
00:05:00,060 --> 00:05:00,920
That's what they say.

157
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,720
With fried shrimp,

158
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:03,960
I usually just eat the whole thing.

159
00:05:05,240 --> 00:05:05,960
You can have this.

160
00:05:05,960 --> 00:05:06,760
It's got fried shrimp.

161
00:05:09,400 --> 00:05:10,200
Yeah, I think the shrimp

162
00:05:10,200 --> 00:05:11,640
turned out pretty well.

163
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:16,440
(Asks)
Can you handle roller coasters?

164
00:05:16,840 --> 00:05:17,840
Easy.

165
00:05:17,840 --> 00:05:18,640
Easy?

166
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,080
But I think pirate ships

167
00:05:21,080 --> 00:05:22,080
are actually pretty scary.

168
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:23,960
When I was little,

169
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,480
like really little,

170
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,160
on the pirate ship,

171
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:29,280
I just

172
00:05:29,280 --> 00:05:30,800
started crying on it.

173
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:31,840
(Cracks up)

174
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:32,999
- When you were little?
- Yeah, really little.

175
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:33,320
Yeah.

176
00:05:33,640 --> 00:05:34,160
I was on it,

177
00:05:34,160 --> 00:05:35,360
and every time it swung,

178
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,840
I'd cry.

179
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:37,840
(Laughing together)

180
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,360
Let me off!

181
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,520
But it couldn't stop.

182
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,040
So I just kept crying.

183
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,880
(Asks)
Do you ever miss Shenyang food?

184
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:48,400
There's a Caida Night Market
in Shenyang.

185
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,480
Have you been?

186
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,520
Caida Night Market?

187
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:51,560
I went once before.

188
00:05:51,560 --> 00:05:53,000
Was the food good?

189
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,040
Some of it was.

190
00:05:54,040 --> 00:05:55,920
But I didn't try everything.

191
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:56,880
They have this thing

192
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:57,960
called a cold noodle wrap.

193
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:58,640
Have you had it?

194
00:05:59,720 --> 00:06:00,520
It's so good.

195
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:01,360
Yeah.

196
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,560
Whenever I'm passing through Shenyang,

197
00:06:02,560 --> 00:06:03,560
I always wanna get one.

198
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,920
If we get the chance next time,

199
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:06,360
I can take you guys there.

200
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:06,920
To Shenyang?

201
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:07,200
Yeah.

202
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:07,680
What?

203
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:08,000
Where?

204
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:08,720
(Curious)

205
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:10,360
Have you guys had a cold noodle wrap?

206
00:06:10,360 --> 00:06:11,160
A cold noodle wrap?

207
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:13,920
Yeah. It's wrapped
in a cold noodle sheet.

208
00:06:13,920 --> 00:06:15,560
There's stinky tofu inside.

209
00:06:15,560 --> 00:06:17,280
You can add sauce or skip it.

210
00:06:17,280 --> 00:06:17,800
Yeah.

211
00:06:17,800 --> 00:06:19,000
And add other toppings.

212
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:20,360
(Blueberries)
You put blueberries in it?

213
00:06:20,360 --> 00:06:21,840
You put blueberries inside?

214
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:23,400
(Totally lost)

215
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:24,400
No blueberries.

216
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:25,360
No.

217
00:06:26,440 --> 00:06:27,520
Stinky tofu.

218
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:29,880
I thought

219
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,280
we were still talking about blueberries.

220
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:33,480
Grilled cold noodles with blueberries.

221
00:06:34,240 --> 00:06:34,800
I was thinking,

222
00:06:34,800 --> 00:06:35,920
stinky tofu,

223
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,920
blueberries, and grilled
cold noodles together?

224
00:06:43,480 --> 00:06:44,440
Okay.

225
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,440
It's nice coming out here to relax.

226
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,720
It's been so long since I've had

227
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:52,360
a chance to camp and barbecue outdoors.

228
00:06:52,360 --> 00:06:54,080
It's been ages.

229
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:58,960
You don't get many chances like this.

230
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:00,160
Yeah, definitely.

231
00:07:01,080 --> 00:07:02,040
It's so quiet.

232
00:07:02,960 --> 00:07:06,000
It's that feeling of getting away
from the city...

233
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:07,400
And just clearing your mind.

234
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:07,920
Yeah.

235
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,000
Just zoning out.

236
00:07:13,640 --> 00:07:16,440
I always look
for really quiet places like this.

237
00:07:16,440 --> 00:07:17,600
- To be by yourself.
- Yeah.

238
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:17,880
Exactly.

239
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:19,280
Because there's none of that

240
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,440
city background noise.

241
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,320
There's always noise in the city.

242
00:07:22,320 --> 00:07:23,080
Clear your mind.

243
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:23,440
Yeah.

244
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:25,600
But there's none of that here.

245
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,720
(Asks)
So you like forests,

246
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:28,520
grasslands?

247
00:07:30,080 --> 00:07:31,720
Forests, grasslands,

248
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:32,920
anywhere near water.

249
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:33,600
I love the ocean.

250
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:37,160
Do you guys prefer the beach,

251
00:07:37,160 --> 00:07:37,920
or something

252
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,160
like open grasslands?

253
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:40,120
Which do you prefer?

254
00:07:40,120 --> 00:07:42,080
Anywhere that's not too dry

255
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:42,880
works for me.

256
00:07:42,880 --> 00:07:43,760
I prefer humid places.

257
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:44,560
What about Beijing?

258
00:07:45,680 --> 00:07:46,640
Beijing's pretty dry.

259
00:07:46,640 --> 00:07:47,760
Yeah, I was gonna say.

260
00:07:49,040 --> 00:07:49,520
It is.

261
00:07:49,520 --> 00:07:50,240
You're used to it now.

262
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:51,280
Yeah.

263
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,320
I've been there too long.

264
00:07:54,880 --> 00:07:56,160
(Asks)
Do you like zoos?

265
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:56,800
I do.

266
00:07:57,560 --> 00:07:58,920
I love going to the zoo.

267
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,600
The zoo?

268
00:07:59,600 --> 00:08:01,320
Yeah, it's so much fun.

269
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:02,960
Aquariums too.

270
00:08:04,400 --> 00:08:05,920
You know that aquarium in Beijing?

271
00:08:06,400 --> 00:08:07,960
That whale is super smart.

272
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:09,160
Really?

273
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,360
It's this huge whale.

274
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,080
Everyone can see it through the glass.

275
00:08:12,080 --> 00:08:13,440
There's this

276
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:14,560
curved glass section.

277
00:08:14,560 --> 00:08:16,640
It presses its face right up

278
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:17,600
against the curved part

279
00:08:17,600 --> 00:08:18,800
and plays with everyone.

280
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:19,800
It even teases the kids.

281
00:08:20,320 --> 00:08:21,120
It's hilarious.

282
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:22,760
It's amazing.

283
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:23,360
So smart.

284
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,160
Bring the guitar over.

285
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:33,360
Time to show off.

286
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:34,159
There's a guitar.

287
00:08:35,230 --> 00:08:37,039
What do you guys wanna sing?

288
00:08:37,039 --> 00:08:37,280
Sure.

289
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,080
Can we really request songs?

290
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:38,840
Of course.

291
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:39,880
Come on, let's play.

292
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:40,159
Here.

293
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:41,320
Can I try it?

294
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,240
I wanna check out the guitar.

295
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:42,919
Here.

296
00:08:44,240 --> 00:08:45,920
You can search for a song.

